1. WHAT THIS IS

The source code, documentation and other files in this repository ("the Software") are
published so that anyone can read them, audit them and report problems. This is
source-available software, not open-source software. The Owner keeps all rights that this
license does not grant.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT A PAID LICENSE

a. Read, study and audit the source code, and quote short parts of it to discuss or report
   a problem.

b. Install and run an official, unmodified release of the Software, for yourself or your
   own organization, with the free tier that the Software itself applies when no license
   key or token is installed, and with the 30-day trial that the Software gives every
   install. The free tier and the trial have the limits written in docs/pricing.md. You
   may run the Software like this for your own VPN store.

c. Modify a copy of the Software on your own computer to evaluate it, to develop it or to
   prepare a contribution to the Owner. The modified copy stays on your own computers: you
   may not run it in production for customers and you may not distribute it.

d. Fork the repository on GitHub, as far as GitHub's Terms of Service give you that right,
   to propose a change back to the Owner. [LAWYER: confirm how this interacts with the
   rest of this license.]

3. WHAT NEEDS A PAID LICENSE

Anything not allowed in section 2 needs a written license from the Owner. In particular,
without a paid license you may not:

a. Go beyond the free tier once the trial is over. A paid license is a license key or a
   signed license token issued by the Owner (see section 4). The paid tiers, and what each
   one allows, are listed in docs/pricing.md.

b. Copy or redistribute the Software, in whole or in part, modified or not, in source or
   in binary form. This includes mirrors, forks published outside GitHub, container images
   and packages that you publish.

c. Distribute a modified version of the Software, or run a modified version in production.

d. Run the Software in production for anyone other than yourself or your own organization.
   This includes hosting it for other operators, managed services, and installing and
   running it for clients as an agency or a reseller of installs.

e. Resell, sublicense, rent or lease the Software or a license key, or offer the Software
   itself, or access to it, as your own product or service.

f. White-label the Software: remove or replace the BOBRES name, mascot and "Powered by
   BOBRES" attribution. White-labelling is a feature of a paid tier that includes it.

g. Remove, hide or change a copyright or license notice in the Software.

h. Disable, bypass, tamper with or work around the Software's license checks and its free
   tier limits, or make or use a license key or token that the Owner did not issue.

4. PAID LICENSES

A paid license is granted by the Owner in a separate agreement (the Terms of Service for
BOBRES operators, docs/legal/terms-of-service.md, once in force, and the order or invoice).
It is proved by a license key or a license token that the Owner signs. Its scope, its
limits and its length are those of its tier and of that agreement. A paid license ends when
the agreement ends or when its payment lapses; the Software then goes back to the free
tier, and nothing that you stored in it is deleted.

